<title>USA: Waste Management gets Bronx contract.</title>
<headline>Waste Management gets Bronx contract.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill. 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Waste Management Inc said Tuesday it won a three-year contract to transfer and dispose of 1,750 tons a day of residential waste from the Bronx in New York City.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Waste Management said it has begun improvements on its Bronx transfer station, where the waste will be handled. The station is permitted to handle up to 2,000 tons a day.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
